Z||000006||turbo86se||08-14-2000||11:31 PM||||Thanks for the compliments guys! I really apprecieate it! I only take my baby out on special occasion, never in the rain. I got lucky in Williamsburg, didn't rain once, and she slept in the garage at my parents house in MD! This summer I have been nearly Fieroless, my mechanic should be getting the V6 in my 88 coupe soon, so I'll be driving a Fiero everyday again! <P>Robertvol, maybe we could "trade" Fieros for a weekend or two. I'd love to drive your 88 GT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Mattsfiero, you'll get it there! Be patient!<P>Jonathon, what Fiero were you driving in Williamsburg? Did I meet you? I'd love to see your pics, but for some reason I can't download them.<P>My7Fieros, yeah I can't wait to get the strut assemblies! I wish my roommate was into Fieros, I'm stuck with a non-cleaning, complaining all the time 22-year old girl, who says the F word about 40 times a minute! At least she doesn't go into my garage! Oh yeah, you're a cop, right? I'll have my associates in Criminal Justice next year, and I'm very interested in Law Enforcement. I'm hopeing to work for County Police, the only part I'm worried about is the interview, what they ask and what they want to hear. Any pointers? Ask Nick if he can send some pics of the Fieros with the struts! TIA!<p>[This message has been edited by turbo86se (edited 08-14-2000).]||||reg||1
